course: dictionary
lesson: 8330
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word roll has many meanings, so context tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it. «Before digital cameras, a roll often had only 24 or 36 pictures.» Here a roll is a long strip of film wound into a tube, because photos were taken on film.
explain: Now look at the sentence: «Wombats leave their cube-shaped droppings on rocks and logs, because the droppings do not roll away.» Roll means to turn over and over, or to move along on wheels or a round shape. The clue is that the droppings are cube-shaped, so they do not move along the ground.
explain: Sometimes roll is a sound. «A roll of thunder shook the house.» Thunder is loud and deep, so a roll means a long, deep sound. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Roll can be a verb (to roll) or a noun (a roll).
fact: «Roll» means to turn over and over, like a ball moving along the ground.
fact: «A roll» can be a small round bread, or a long piece of film, paper or tape wound into a tube.
fact: «A roll» can also be a list of names, like the class roll, or a long deep sound, like a drum roll.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning of roll, so check the words around it.
exercise: «Before digital cameras, a roll often had only 24 or 36 pictures.» What is a roll here? | A long deep sound | A list of names | *A long strip of film wound into a tube | A small round bread
exercise: «Wombats leave their cube-shaped droppings on rocks and logs, because the droppings do not roll away.» What does roll mean here? | *Move along the ground | Sing loudly | Eat up | Cook slowly
exercise: Mrs Lee calls the roll at the start of the day. What is the roll? | A long deep sound | A small round bread | *A list of names | A roll of paper towel
test: «Roll up your sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» What does roll up mean here? | Listen to them | Roll them along the floor | *Fold them up neatly | Throw them away
test: Jade rolls the dice and gets a six. What does rolls mean? | *Throws | Counts | Hides | Bakes
exam: «In the story, a roll of thunder shook the house.» What does roll mean? | A list of names | *A long, deep sound | Small round bread | Turning over and over
